Generic single-database configuration with async support.

## Common Alembic Commands

### Generate a new migration
```bash
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "description of changes"
```

### Apply all pending migrations
```bash
alembic upgrade head
```

### Rollback one migration
```bash
alembic downgrade -1
```

### View current migration version
```bash
alembic current
```

### View migration history
```bash
alembic history --verbose
```

### Rollback to a specific revision
```bash
alembic downgrade <revision_id>
```

### Upgrade to a specific revision
```bash
alembic upgrade <revision_id>
```

## Notes

- This configuration uses async SQLAlchemy with asyncpg for PostgreSQL
- The DATABASE_URL is automatically loaded from app.core.config.settings
- All models are imported in env.py to ensure complete schema detection
- Migrations support both online (connected) and offline (SQL script) modes
